{
  "findings": [
    {
      "title": "[P2] Read preloaded capabilities from every compatibility target",
      "body": "When a same-origin sandbox splits ChatGPT globals—for example, `window.openai` contains cached `widgetState` while `window.parent.openai` already contains only `toolResponseMetadata`—`currentOpenAiGlobals()` selects the widget-state candidate and this reads the capability from only that object. If no later `openai:set_globals` event fires and host `toolInfo` is absent, restoration has neither an ID nor capability, so pagination/disclosure state cannot restore or save. Combine preloaded data and metadata across all compatibility targets.",
      "confidence_score": 0.98,
      "priority": 2,
      "code_location": {
        "absolute_file_path": "/Users/burakemre/Code/lobu/.claude/worktrees/mcp-app-v8/packages/owletto/src/mcp-apps/_shared/host.tsx",
        "line_range": {
          "start": 546,
          "end": 547
        }
      }
    },
    {
      "title": "[P2] Persist edits after late identity restoration",
      "body": "When a card is initially loaded only from cached `widgetState`, `hasLiveToolOutput` remains false. If the user changes view state before late capability metadata arrives, the original save timer runs without an identity and is dropped; restoration then correctly merges the edit, but this guard suppresses persistence and no later trigger saves it, so the edit is lost on reload. Persist successful restores when local view-state revisions exist, and apply the same correction to the equivalent host-context/connect guards.",
      "confidence_score": 0.99,
